> 
> The game needs to access the file in your home directory, but the binary
> is normally set up with suid games, sometimse sgid bin. So you need to
> give the world x right to your home directory and r right to the file.
> chmod a+x ~
> chmod a+r ~/.nethackrc
> 
> Notice that just giving x rights to a directory doesn't give the right
> to read the directory listing, just to open files by name to those who
> already know the name of the file to read, so this is normally not a big
> security risk if you don't keep anything secret directly in your home
> directory. If you are paranoid about that, you may want to move your
> most sensitive files to some subdirectory that doesn't have x rights
> given to the world.
> The .nethackrc file probably doesn't include anything you need to keep
> secret.

